    "title": "subject + 将 + affected object + predicate",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk4-prepositions-p06-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "subject + 将 + affected object + predicate",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Formal object-marking 将 places an identifiable affected object before its result-bearing predicate. It differs from future 将 directly before a verb.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "请将书放在桌子上。",
                "pinyin": "qǐng jiāng shū fàng zài zhuōzi shàng 。",
                "meaning": "Please put the book on the table.",
                "audio": "d05c351e9da893995989acf8cf3b150260a47f569169c75aee783468b8b50ed1"
              },
              {
                "text": "他将门关上了。",
                "pinyin": "tā jiāng mén guān shàng le 。",
                "meaning": "He closed the door.",
                "audio": "bf8a8860ce0bc1060c03906cb2345a92417079901999c12a13b2de9b6b38e8f6"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
